{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>Would that their heart were always like this, to fear Me</b> — since man's free will is in his hand to merit or to incur guilt, and all is in the hands of Heaven except fear of Heaven, Scripture says thus, and it is in human language. And by way of truth, it is like (Job 28:28), 'And He said to man: Behold, fear of Adonai is wisdom, and to depart from evil is understanding.' And so they said concerning the reward of mitzvot (Menachot 29b): He saw them combbing the flesh of Rabbi Akiva with iron combs; he said to Him, 'Master of the Universe, this is Torah and this is its reward?' The Holy One, blessed be He, answered him, 'Silence — thus it arose in thought before Me.' And you will understand this from what He said (Deuteronomy 5:28), 'But as for you, stand here by Me,'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {0 "The verse quoted from Job 28:28 uses the divine name אֲדֹנָי, rendered here as Adonai per the divine-name convention."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:45:48.351097696Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}